# ESP32-S3 Arduino matrix L5_adc, before/after the A0 fix (2026-11-08)
# board esp32s3 (PlatformIO esp32-s3-devkitc-1, espressif32 8.0.0 / arduino-esp32 3.3.12 locally;
#   CI pins espressif32@7.0.1). labwired: target/debug/labwired at 848cca640 + this change.
# Run to the 50M-step limit with stop_when_assertions_pass: false so the LW_L5_VAL line is captured.

## BEFORE (sketch read analogRead(0): defined(A0) is false on arduino-esp32, GPIO0 is not an ADC pin on the S3)
LW_L5_BOOT
LW_L5_OK
LW_L5_VAL 0 0
# -> passed because the generic oracle accepts any equal pair; nothing converted.

## AFTER (A0 = GPIO1 = ADC1_CH0 via the RTC SAR / esp32s3_sens; oracle requires exact 2048)
LW_L5_BOOT
LW_L5_OK
LW_L5_VAL 2048 2048
status: pass

## matrix runner (run_matrix.py --boards esp32s3 --sketches L5_adc)
==> esp32s3 × L5_adc
    compile: ok (firmware.elf)
    run: pass

## classic ESP32 row, same sketch, unchanged (GPIO0 = ADC2_CH1 there, really converts)
LW_L5_BOOT
LW_L5_OK
LW_L5_VAL 529 529

